  "reading": {
   "title": "Hafsa's new city",
   "text": "Hafsa lives in a small city. The city has a river, a big library and a famous bridge. Tourists often take photos of the bridge. Downtown, there is a market on Saturdays. Hafsa buys fruit and bread there.\n\nHer neighborhood is safe and friendly. There is a school at the end of the street, and a hospital is near it. Hafsa goes to the library every week, because the library has free English classes. The traffic in the morning is bad, so she usually walks.\n\nOn weekends, Hafsa and Emre often walk along the river and sit in the park. Sometimes they eat ice cream near the bridge. Isparta is smaller, and she misses it sometimes. But Hafsa likes her new city too. \"It isn't Isparta,\" she says, \"but it's home now.\"",
